route-selected-proxy-through-outbound-clients

Lane: cross

Unit: configure-application-proxy-at-runtime

ChildPatch: route-selected-proxy-through-outbound-clients

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema-snapshot

Purpose: Configure and switch application-process outbound HTTP and WebSocket proxies through the control center without changing shell networking.

Requires: Unit:cross/host-dialogs-with-shared-resources

Provides: Persist private proxy.json entries and selected enablement, load before server bootstrap, validate and atomically save before activation, publish proxy/read, proxy/write and proxy/updated, route through native HTTP pools and WebSocket connectors with local and reserved IPv4/IPv6 bypass, invalidate reused connections after changes, and provide app-scoped selected proxy observations, shared-resource staged picker and prompt constructors independent of ChatWidget, and bounded identity probes.

Boundary: Native destination policy, authentication, TLS and disabled proxy routing remain authoritative; shell environment and sandbox egress are unchanged, invalid configuration or failed persistence does not silently disable routing, probe credentials stay out of diagnostics, and no legacy proxy format reader is retained. Cross dialog resources own input preferences and the centered stack lifecycle; this Unit owns proxy content, configuration callbacks and its ordinary host integration. Control-center layout, shortcuts and its independent dialog host remain with its interface consumer; no private slash-command or status-line entrypoints are added.

Verification: Retain HTTP routing, protocol, startup, persistence, WebSocket switching and bypass coverage. Focused TUI tests verify global observations, bootstrap failures, real RPC round trips, independent shared-resource dialog construction, configured input, staged picker callbacks and cancellation without requiring ChatWidget modal state.

CrossGroup: control-center


